<title>HONG KONG: Tristate interim net down 44.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Tristate interim net down 44.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   25.0	vs 44.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    10.0	vs 15.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  6.94 loss vs 13.37 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    30.48     vs 54.69</p>
<p>    Turnover		     603.83    vs 575.01</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tristate Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 24 to October 1</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 1</p>
<p>NOTE - Tristate is a garment manufacturer.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on the group's factories in the Philippines laid off about 1,100 employees and redundancy payments of HK$6.9 million had been made.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
